# OpenCart Playwright TypeScript Automation

This repository is a **Playwright/TypeScript test automation framework** for the [OpenCart demo store](https://awesomeqa.com/ui/). It is **not** a full-stack application under test — it is the automation system itself.

## Purpose

Demonstrate Staff-level QA engineering through:

- Feature-module architecture (presentation / state / services)
- Layered Playwright tests (functional, integration, E2E, API, hybrid)
- Reusable `@opencart-auto/pw-core` workspace package
- CI/CD, Docker, and AI-assisted test workflows (`.github/agents/`)

## Documentation hierarchy (source of truth)

1. [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) — structure, diagrams, import rules
2. [docs/adr/](../docs/adr/) — architectural decisions
3. [README.md](../README.md) — setup and commands
4. [specs/test.plan.md](../specs/test.plan.md) — test scenarios

## Repository layout (summary)

```
src/features/<name>/   presentation · state · services (per domain)
src/shared/            routes and HTTP types only
src/fixtures/          Playwright fixture wiring
src/tests/             functional | integration | e2e | api | hybrid
packages/pw-core/      BasePage, assertions, Wait, shared interfaces
```

**Do not reintroduce** flat `src/pages/`, `src/components/`, `src/data/`, or `src/api/`.

## Core principles

- **Correctness over speed** — changes need tests and verification where behavior changes
- **Architecture over convenience** — respect feature boundaries and layer rules
- **Clarity over complexity** — prefer simple POM and services over clever abstractions
- **Observability over assumption** — verify against the running store when UI/API behavior changes (see `ironbee-devtools-use.mdc`)

## Out of scope

- Building or modifying the OpenCart application itself
- Production trading, financial, or compliance systems
- Sprint/roadmap processes from other templates (this repo uses ADRs + test plan, not product sprints)
